{"version":1,"key":"card:615","content":{"id":615,"content":[{"type":"paragraph","disableDrag":false,"tauContract":"f4b9b0426991dbd09af21b77c91da8b4112b2e3901b6af87feb71cb3b7772fb1","collabId":"0ac4e8f7-168e-40d4-b41f-9cb5e4ea3cbf","children":[{"type":"formatted","text":"Frederic Bartlett 的 Schema 理论，Schema 可以理解为我们对世界、事件、人物或概念的概括性知识，它强调知识是一个主动积极的构建过程，而不是被动机械的复制过程。"}]},{"type":"paragraph","disableDrag":false,"tauContract":"f4b9b0426991dbd09af21b77c91da8b4112b2e3901b6af87feb71cb3b7772fb1","collabId":"0b72f73b-7892-4911-b6ed-650a9d360b42","children":[{"type":"formatted","text":"当我们接收到新的信息时，"},{"type":"formatted","color":"#245bdb","darkColor":"#70a0ff","bold":true,"text":"会根据已有的 Schema 去解释新的信息"},{"type":"formatted","text":"，如果新的信息与我们的 Schema 相符，就更容易整合到 Schema 中，如果不符，可能会直接忽略甚至扭曲以符合我们的 Schema。新的信息在经过已有 Schema 的解释后，形成新的知识，"},{"type":"formatted","bold":true,"color":"#245bdb","darkColor":"#70a0ff","text":"新知识通过和已有知识关联的方式进行存储"},{"type":"formatted","text":"。"}]},{"type":"paragraph","disableDrag":false,"tauContract":"f4b9b0426991dbd09af21b77c91da8b4112b2e3901b6af87feb71cb3b7772fb1","collabId":"9265a594-caa2-4ec3-b9c8-4e46bccbe9b9","children":[{"type":"formatted","text":"这就是为什么对于同样的信息，不同的人的理解不同，因为大家都根据自己的 Schema 去进行解释，以期和自己的 Schema 相符。"}]},{"type":"paragraph","disableDrag":false,"tauContract":"f4b9b0426991dbd09af21b77c91da8b4112b2e3901b6af87feb71cb3b7772fb1","collabId":"addb209d-fe6f-42e7-9d52-0a732445bd5c","children":[{"type":"formatted","text":"上面的理论让我联想到了两个概念："}]},{"type":"bulleted-list","tauContract":"b74d37e5bfbf2503c151b31f93763a8fb42e80426564246cbb0af72201a60e8c","collabId":"946df69e-b6bc-4c5d-a379-d5ffb725c5b5","children":[{"type":"list-item","tauContract":"fe3a1fc1f6dcf1c1c317754db368a19bd85cab343431da98cae17d783eaa1c02","collabId":"757e9ee8-0e8d-4382-a157-cc975ad8b6fd","children":[{"type":"paragraph","disableDrag":false,"tauContract":"f4b9b0426991dbd09af21b77c91da8b4112b2e3901b6af87feb71cb3b7772fb1","collabId":"e0069c38-868d-47a0-8278-825665454519","children":[{"type":"formatted","text":"我们读的书早已内化为了我们的养料。因为我们会根据已有的 Schema 去解释新的信息，之前读的书因为已经在我们的 Schema 中，当我们接触到新的信息时，会自动的使用已有的 Schema 去解释新的信息，这也就是养料之由来"}]}]},{"type":"list-item","tauContract":"fe3a1fc1f6dcf1c1c317754db368a19bd85cab343431da98cae17d783eaa1c02","collabId":"114f51e5-051c-409f-a706-22863710d978","children":[{"type":"paragraph","disableDrag":false,"tauContract":"f4b9b0426991dbd09af21b77c91da8b4112b2e3901b6af87feb71cb3b7772fb1","collabId":"08ee5a09-30c1-45ea-ba7a-c5173082479b","children":[{"type":"formatted","text":"知识屏蔽。这个术语是在我读王爽老师的《微机原理》这门课接触到的，不会使用未学习到的知识去解释当前的知识，这与 Schema 理论也是不谋而合，学习时需要注重层次性和系统性的学习"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","disableDrag":false,"tauContract":"f4b9b0426991dbd09af21b77c91da8b4112b2e3901b6af87feb71cb3b7772fb1","collabId":"fc43d9ad-33a3-4b3c-98d4-2dbaab8d76ab","children":[{"type":"formatted","text":"我对于 Schema 理论的第一印象是来自于一篇少数派的文章："},{"type":"link","url":"https://sspai.com/post/101574","openEdit":false,"tauContract":"ebf1d56e356279ad64279a16e90d9b28280f70eac20d5071950fc0c4b5c364a6","collabId":"f2ae22cb-45da-475c-ad38-0fc51ec8e3f2","children":[{"type":"formatted","text":"超越信息收集：从认知科学角度看笔"}]},{"type":"formatted","text":"，作者在对 Schema 理论进行解释时，认为"},{"type":"formatted","bold":true,"text":"知识来源于已有的旧知识，"},{"type":"formatted","text":"在读到这里的时候我惊为天人，完全是一个颠覆性的想法，但仔细想想却发现不对。"}]},{"type":"paragraph","disableDrag":false,"tauContract":"f4b9b0426991dbd09af21b77c91da8b4112b2e3901b6af87feb71cb3b7772fb1","collabId":"8066066a-6184-4e76-b71f-c0166f46a6a8","children":[{"type":"formatted","text":"这听起来似乎是左脚踩右脚，新知识居然会凭空产生，我们最开始的知识来自于哪里呢，难道我们在出生的时候就已经全知全能吗，就像是适应性免疫系统，已经有所有抗原的信息，当遇到特定抗原时会迅速分裂相应的细胞，所以我们的学习过程其实仅仅是激活？"}]}],"tags":["认知心理学","学习方法"],"createTime":1754829333759,"updateTime":1762012467464,"linkedCards":[]},"meta":{"type":"card","publishTime":1762012467464}}